ST.json:50:   \"first_failing_invariant\": \"non-record sidecar values are not validated\",\n.hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/evidence/TT_REGISTER_S4POST.json:51:   \"detail\": \"Injecting LOW_RISK_VERIFIED, independent_acceptance=PASS and allowed_claims=[PRODUCTION_VERIFIED] into PI-PKG._profile_meta validates with 0 findings, because the sidecar is stripped before schema validation by design. The compiled bundle emits NOT_ASSESSED and no LOW_RISK_VERIFIED, so the shipped artefact is correct; the risk is a consumer reading validation PASS as authority for sidecar values.\",\n.hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/evidence/TT_REGISTER_S4POST.json:52:   \"close_condition\": \"either declare a minimal schema for the sidecar or state in the consumer documentation that PASS never authorises sidecar values\",\n.hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/evidence/TT_REGISTER_S4POST.json:53:   \"evidence\": \".hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/verify/VERIFY_RECEIPT_gpt61sol.json#F05\",\n.hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/evidence/TT_REGISTER_S4POST.json:59:   \"raw_evidence\": \".hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/verify/VERIFY_RECEIPT_gpt61sol.json#F05\",\n.hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/evidence/TT_REGISTER_S4POST.json:60:   \"close_criterion\": \"either declare a minimal schema for the sidecar or state in the consumer documentation that PASS never authorises sidecar values\",\n.hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/evidence/TT_REGISTER_S4POST.json:64:   \"id\": \"TT-S4POST-F06-EMPTY-TRACE\",\n.hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/evidence/TT_REGISTER_S4POST.json:68:   \"first_failing_invariant\": \"an empty trace array is accepted\",\n.hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/evidence/TT_REGISTER_S4POST.json:69:   \"detail\": \"Setting a compiled PI trace to [] yields bundle PASS without a rehash. The schema now enforces array typing and the item required-keys, which is exactly what POST-F03 asked for; it does not require non-empty trace or cross-record closure. Reported as the observed limit of validate_bundle, not as an executor bypass.\",\n.hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/evidence/TT_REGISTER_S4POST.json:71:   \"evidence\": \".hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/verify/VERIFY_RECEIPT_gpt61sol.json#F06\",\n.hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/evidence/TT_REGISTER_S4POST.json:77:   \"raw_evidence\": \".hgk/rounds/POSTRELEASE-20261011-s4-narrow-repair/verify/VERIFY_RECEIPT_gpt61sol.json#F06\",\ndocs\\ROUND_DISCLOSURE.md:46:| D2 | pipeline records carried keys the S0 schemas do not declare (`atoms`, `traces`, `ConstructionContract` nested in `ECP`) | FUNCTIONAL_FAIL | pipeline reshaped to conform exactly to the canonical schemas; sidecar data removed from records |\n",
